---
import ContentLayout from '../../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: 'Website Audit', href: '/website-audit/' },
  { label: 'Checklists', href: '/website-audit-checklist/' },
  { label: 'Template', href: '/website-audit-checklist/template/' },
];
const toc = [
  { label: 'Download the PDF', id: 'download' },
  { label: "What's Included", id: 'whats-included' },
  { label: 'How to Use It', id: 'how-to-use-it' },
  { label: 'Scoring Guide', id: 'scoring-guide' },
  { label: 'Customisation Tips', id: 'customisation-tips' },
];
---
<ContentLayout
  title="Website Audit Template: Free 50-Check PDF Download"
  description="Download a free printable website audit template with 50 checks, an evidence-based scoring guide and an action plan. No email required."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  toc={toc}
  publishDate="2026-03-28"
>
  <p>This free <strong>website audit template</strong> provides 50 manual checks across technical SEO, on-page SEO, content quality and off-page signals. Use the printable PDF to record scores and connect findings to an action plan. No email or account is required.</p>

  <h2 id="download">Download the Website Audit Template</h2>
  <p>The PDF includes a scoring guide, four checklists and an action-plan worksheet. It is a manual review aid. It does not scan your website or calculate scores automatically.</p>
  <p><a href="/downloads/auditweb-website-audit-checklist.pdf" download>Download the 50-check website audit template (PDF)</a></p>
  <p>Version: 5 September 2026. The template is free for personal and commercial use. You may adapt and redistribute it. Attribution to AuditWeb is appreciated.</p>

  <p>For editable working documents, download the <a href="/resources/agency-audit-toolkit/">agency report template and implementation tracker</a>.</p>
  <h2 id="whats-included">What's Included?</h2>
  <p>The template contains four sections. Each check has an ID, a description of the evidence to review, a suggested method and space for a score.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Technical SEO: 15 checks.</strong> Review crawl access, indexing, response codes, Core Web Vitals, HTTPS, mobile usability, structured data, redirects, sitemaps, robots directives, rendered content, server reliability, site architecture, duplicate URLs and international pages.</li>
    <li><strong>On-page SEO: 12 checks.</strong> Review titles, descriptions, headings, internal links, images, canonical tags, URL structure, social previews, breadcrumbs, search intent, priority-page access and broken links.</li>
    <li><strong>Content quality: 13 checks.</strong> Review answer completeness, search intent, competing pages, freshness, evidence, low-value pages, repeated content, readability, topic coverage, demand gaps, useful media, next actions and engagement measurement.</li>
    <li><strong>Off-page signals: 10 checks.</strong> Review referring sites, anchor context, suspicious links, link changes, competitor sources, brand mentions, local information, reviews, official profiles and the limits of third-party authority scores.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The action-plan worksheet connects a check ID and affected URL to a finding, proposed fix, owner, deadline and verification step.</p>

  <h2 id="how-to-use-it">How to Use the Template</h2>
  <p>Define the review scope before scoring. Record the website, reviewer, review date and sampled URLs on the first page.</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Gather evidence.</strong> Use Search Console and a crawl where available. Inspect important pages and customer journeys in a browser.</li>
    <li><strong>Work through the checks.</strong> Start with technical access. Continue through on-page SEO and content. Finish with off-page evidence.</li>
    <li><strong>Record findings.</strong> Note each check ID alongside the affected URL and the observation that supports your score. Mark unavailable checks as not checked.</li>
    <li><strong>Assign actions.</strong> Give each priority fix an owner and a verification step. Recheck the affected page after implementation.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Read additional context on individual checks in the <a href="/website-audit-checklist/seo/">SEO audit checklist</a>. Review a worked report structure in the <a href="/website-audit-services/report-example/">website audit report example</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="scoring-guide">How Should You Score a Website Audit?</h2>
  <p>Score each completed check from 0 to 3 using evidence from the reviewed scope. Leave untested checks blank and mark inapplicable checks N/A.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>0: Critical failure.</strong> Evidence shows a serious problem requiring attention.</li>
    <li><strong>1: Significant issue.</strong> A meaningful problem needs investigation or a fix.</li>
    <li><strong>2: Improvement needed.</strong> A specific improvement remains.</li>
    <li><strong>3: Meets the check.</strong> The reviewed scope meets the stated check.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Calculate the score as <strong>sum of numeric scores ÷ (3 × number of scored checks) × 100</strong>. Exclude N/A and untested checks from that calculation. Leave the score blank if no checks have been scored.</p>
  <p>Report completion separately as <strong>scored checks ÷ applicable checks</strong>. Scoring 10 checks at 3 gives a score of 100%. Completion is only 20% when all 50 checks apply. That is a partial audit.</p>
  <p>A high average score does not cancel a critical finding. These scores organise your review; they do not predict rankings, revenue or legal compliance.</p>

  <h2 id="customisation-tips">How Can You Adapt the Template?</h2>
  <p>Adapt the scope to the website. Add checkout tests for an online shop or enquiry-form tests for a service business. Mark local and international checks N/A when they do not apply.</p>
  <p>Verify time-sensitive standards before each review. The PDF links to primary guidance on SEO fundamentals, Core Web Vitals, robots.txt and canonical URLs.</p>
  <p>Get help interpreting the evidence and deciding which fixes to commission through our <a href="/website-audit-services/">professional website audit services</a> for the available scope and next steps.</p>
</ContentLayout>
